## Key Audit Findings

### 1. Cold Load & FCP on Fast 3G (Threshold: 2.50s) — `FAIL`
- **Measurement Profile:** Emulated Chrome Fast 3G (1.6 Mbps download, 750 kbps upload, 150 ms RTT) via CDP `Network.emulateNetworkConditions` on a cold cache across 3 consecutive runs:
  - **Run 1:** Load = `30,516.8 ms` (30.52s), Transfer = `7,594,167 bytes`
  - **Run 2:** Load = `30,518.1 ms` (30.52s), Transfer = `7,594,167 bytes`
  - **Run 3:** Load = `30,525.8 ms` (30.53s), Transfer = `7,594,167 bytes`
  - **Average:** **30.52 seconds** (exceeds budget by **+28.02 seconds**; >12× over budget).
- **Unthrottled Loopback Baseline:** Run 1 = `360 ms`, Run 2 = `460 ms`, Run 3 = `372 ms` (Average FCP: `397 ms` / 0.40s).
- **Root Cause:** The target web server (`Python SimpleHTTP/0.6`) serves files without `Content-Encoding` (no gzip or brotli). Transferring the uncompressed **6.29 MB** bundle over a 1.6 Mbps link takes ~30.5s before JS execution begins.
- **Evidence:** [`reports/audit/evidence/S7/cold_load_fast3g.json`](file:///home/ubuntu/apps/islamic_app/reports/audit/evidence/S7/cold_load_fast3g.json) and [`reports/audit/evidence/S7/raw_metrics_repeatability.txt`](file:///home/ubuntu/apps/islamic_app/reports/audit/evidence/S7/raw_metrics_repeatability.txt).

### 2. JavaScript Bundle Size & Serving Audit — `FAIL`
- **On-Disk Assets:**
  - `index-*.js`: **6,285,990 bytes** (5.995 MB raw | 1.366 MB gzip | 0.888 MB brotli)
  - `worker-*.js`: **132,625 bytes** (0.126 MB raw | 0.034 MB gzip | 0.029 MB brotli)
  - **Total JS:** **6,418,615 bytes** (6.121 MB raw | 1.400 MB gzip | 0.917 MB brotli)
- **Code-Splitting Assessment:** No dynamic route-level code splitting was found in `dist/_expo/static/js/web/`. All 52 screens, modules, and dependencies are packed into one initial bundle.
- **Evidence:** [`reports/audit/evidence/S7/js_bundle_analysis.json`](file:///home/ubuntu/apps/islamic_app/reports/audit/evidence/S7/js_bundle_analysis.json).

### 3. Long-List DOM Node Counts & Scroll Performance — `PASS`
- **Surahs List (114 Surahs, `quran/home`):**
  - Initial DOM nodes: `3,509` → Post-scroll DOM nodes: `4,169` (+660 nodes rendered as user scrolled down).
  - Average FPS: **60 FPS** (30 frames in 486.6 ms), with 11 dropped frames (>16.7 ms) and 0 jank frames (>33.3 ms).
- **Hadith Library (Books / Collections, `library/hadith`):**
  - Initial DOM nodes: `4,431` → Post-scroll DOM nodes: `4,431` (+0 delta).
  - *Architecture Note:* Uses unwindowed `DetailScreen.ScrollView` with `collections.map(...)`; all collections mount upfront.
  - Average FPS: **60 FPS** (30 frames in 490.6 ms), with 11 dropped frames (>16.7 ms) and 0 jank frames.
- **99 Names of Allah (`library/names`):**
  - Initial DOM nodes: `4,425` → Post-scroll DOM nodes: `4,613` (+188 nodes).
  - Average FPS: **60 FPS** (30 frames in 494.9 ms), with 12 dropped frames (>16.7 ms) and 1 jank frame (34 ms).
- **Evidence:** [`reports/audit/evidence/S7/long_list_scroll_performance.json`](file:///home/ubuntu/apps/islamic_app/reports/audit/evidence/S7/long_list_scroll_performance.json).

### 4. Responsiveness, Dropped Frames & Long Tasks — `PASS`
- **Captured Long Tasks:** 4 tasks >50 ms total:
  - Hydration / bundle parse: `177 ms` and `99 ms`.
  - Component initialization: `56 ms` and `65 ms`.
- **Total Blocking Time (TBT):** **197 ms** (well within the ≤200 ms standard for web applications).
- **Evidence:** [`reports/audit/evidence/S7/dropped_frames_long_tasks.json`](file:///home/ubuntu/apps/islamic_app/reports/audit/evidence/S7/dropped_frames_long_tasks.json).

### 5. Navigation Memory Growth Soak & Browser Limitations — `PASS`
- **Methodology & Limitation:** Headless Chromium was run through **150 continuous navigation cycles** across 8 core routes (`home`, `quran/home`, `quran/reader`, `library/hub`, `library/hadith`, `library/names`, `tools/hub`, `tools/qibla`) over 300 seconds (5 minutes). Headless duration was capped at 300s to avoid CDP session disconnects.
- **Metrics Collected via CDP `Performance.getMetrics`:**
  - **Baseline Heap Used:** `31.76 MB` (3,886 nodes, 1 document).
  - **Heap Trajectory:** Fluctuated between 24 MB and 89 MB as V8 scavenger and mark-sweep garbage collection periodically reclaimed transient memory (e.g. at 96s: 26.3 MB; at 144s: 25.5 MB; at 224s: 24.4 MB).
  - **Final Post-Soak Heap:** `34.41 MB` (net **+2.65 MB** over 150 cycles; growth rate: **0.529 MB/min**).
  - **Projected 10-Minute Growth:** **~5.29 MB** (bounded, stable).
  - **DOM Nodes:** Stabilized between 4,627 and 5,044 after all tabs mounted.
- **Verdict:** Stable; no runaway memory leak during rapid navigation.
- **Evidence:** [`reports/audit/evidence/S7/navigation_memory_soak.json`](file:///home/ubuntu/apps/islamic_app/reports/audit/evidence/S7/navigation_memory_soak.json).

### 6. Interval Leaks After Leaving Home Tab — `FAIL`
- **Registration Trace:** [`HomeScreen.tsx:312`](file:///home/ubuntu/apps/islamic_app/src/screens/HomeScreen.tsx#L312) starts a 30-second interval:
  ```ts
  const id = setInterval(() => setNow(new Date()), 30000);
  ```
- **Lifecycle Defect:** In [`App.tsx:883`](file:///home/ubuntu/apps/islamic_app/App.tsx#L883), tab panes are toggled via CSS display:
  ```tsx
  <View style={[styles.tabPane, tab === 'home' ? styles.paneVisible : styles.paneHidden]}>
  ```
  Because `HomeScreen` is never unmounted when switching to Quran, Library, or Tools, this timer **remains active and continues firing in the background**.
- **Revisit Behavior:** Revisiting Home does not register a duplicate timer (active count remains 1), but background intervals tick indefinitely while hidden.
- **Evidence:** [`reports/audit/evidence/S7/interval_leaks_home.json`](file:///home/ubuntu/apps/islamic_app/reports/audit/evidence/S7/interval_leaks_home.json).

### 7. 3-Minute Monkey Testing per Tab — `PARTIAL (2 PASS / 2 FAIL)`
All four primary tabs were tested concurrently for 180 seconds each (**3,230 total interactive actions**):

| Tab | Duration | Total Actions | Clicks / Scrolls / Keys | White Screens | Uncaught UI Errors | Unhandled Rejections | API Failures | Status |
| :--- | :---: | :---: | :---: | :---: | :---: | :---: | :---: | :---: |
| **Home** | 180s | 820 | 459 / 236 / 125 | 0 | 0 | 0 | 913 | **PASS** |
| **Quran** | 180s | 805 | 461 / 239 / 105 | 0 | 0 | 0 | 1,186 | **PASS** |
| **Library** | 180s | 810 | 450 / 234 / 126 | 0 | 1 | 1 | 1,035 | **FAIL** |
| **Tools** | 180s | 795 | 440 / 234 / 121 | 0 | 1 | 1 | 1,418 | **FAIL** |

- **White Screen Detection:** **0 occurrences** across all 3,230 actions. The root element and navigation dock remained fully rendered.
- **Discovered UI Bug:** In Library and Tools tabs, pressing reminder/snooze elements triggered an unhandled rejection:
  ```text
  The method or property Notifications.scheduleNotificationAsync is not available on web
    at _e.scheduleNotificationAsync
    at _e.snoozePrayer
    at async onPress
  ```
  Missing `Platform.OS !== 'web'` check around native notification scheduling.
- **Evidence:** [`reports/audit/evidence/S7/monkey_testing_tabs.json`](file:///home/ubuntu/apps/islamic_app/reports/audit/evidence/S7/monkey_testing_tabs.json).

### 8. Error Taxonomy: API Failures vs. UI Failures — `PASS`
- **API Network Failures (Isolated):** `4,552` total network error events were captured across the audit (CORS-blocked `ERR_FAILED` requests to `https://api.islamic.app/v1/timings`, `dhikr/after-prayer`, and `hadith/today`). These were handled by application error boundaries/banners and did **not** cause UI crashes or white screens.
- **UI Runtime Failures (Isolated):** Exactly 1 distinct client runtime defect (`Notifications.scheduleNotificationAsync` missing web platform guard), which was tracked separately.
- **Evidence:** Documented in [`reports/audit/S7.json`](file:///home/ubuntu/apps/islamic_app/reports/audit/S7.json#L240-L260).

